# COVERAGE FIXTURE. Deliberate test data, not an ontology about anything.
#
# RULE: cls-avf
# W3C OWL 2 Web Ontology Language Profiles (Second Edition), section 4.3,
# Table 6: The Semantics of Classes.
# https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules
#
#   T(?x, owl:allValuesFrom, ?y)
#   T(?x, owl:onProperty, ?p)
#   T(?u, rdf:type, ?x)
#   T(?u, ?p, ?v)
#     ->  T(?v, rdf:type, ?y)
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. The repository ships allValuesFrom restrictions in its TBoxes
# and instance data that uses the restricted properties, but never both in one
# graph, so tools/horn_differential.py compared the Rust and Python engines on
# cls-avf zero times and its clean sweep said nothing about it.
#
# EXPECTED: exactly one derivation, credited to cls-avf:
#   :y rdf:type :C
#
# The restriction is a NAMED node rather than the blank node OWL would normally
# use. The rule is a triple pattern and does not care, and a named node keeps
# the expected derivation writable here without a blank-node label to track.

@prefix : <http://ex.org/cover/cls-avf#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

:R a owl:Restriction ;
   owl:onProperty :p ;
   owl:allValuesFrom :C .

:x a :R ;
   :p :y .
